    and the verifier still scored reward 0 — the agent validated through
    its own checklist, not the grader's oracle. False = not in the class
    (killed, unmet ledger — that is the gh-1646 surrender class instead —
    or a nonzero reward). None = unclassifiable — a missing ledger or
    verifier-reward input (legacy artifacts) never fabricates the class.

